Chapter: GopFont
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Guios chapter FontLoad
  cites Guios chapter GuiDisplay

 TrueType from the stick -- H4c. The guios font loader carries its
 own FAT32 walk over the block-read-sector syscall, which is dead on
 the Option A path (the stub never installs the syscall machinery
 firmware-side of runtime-init, and the boot medium may not even be
 an IDE disk). But everything after the sector reads is buffer-pure:
 fb-parse-ttf takes a flat byte buffer, fb-render-ascii rasterizes
 from it, fl-raster-to-gobf packs the coverage tables. So the port is
 one seam: read the TTF off the ESP with gfat-read-file-bulk -- the
 same driver stack that already reads the seed, riding the medium
 lock -- and hand the buffer to the unchanged guios pipeline.

 The rasterized font is a GopBitmapFont: 95 glyphs of 8-bit alpha
 coverage plus advance and y-offset tables, drawn by gbf-put-text
 with per-pixel blending against whatever is already on the panel.

 We say:

Section: Font Handle

  GopFont = record {
    gf-ok : Boolean,
    gf-base : Integer,
    gf-gw : Integer,
    gf-gh : Integer
  }

  gfont-none : GopFont
  gfont-none = GopFont { gf-ok = False, gf-base = 0, gf-gw = 0, gf-gh = 0 }

Section: Load

 One flat read, then the guios pipeline verbatim. The glyph pixel
 lists and supersampling scratch this allocates live until the
 caller's heap mark is restored; a desktop session loads once at
 entry and reclaims at exit.

  gfont-load : Fat16Volume, Text -> [Device.Port] GopFont
  gfont-load (vol) (name) = act
    size <- gfat-file-size vol name
    if size == 0 then gfont-none
    else act
      let buf = __heap-save
      in let adv = __heap-advance (size + 1024)
      in act
        n <- gfat-read-file-bulk vol name buf
        if n == 0 then gfont-none
        else let font = fb-parse-ttf buf size
        in let rasters = fb-render-ascii buf font font-ppem
        in let maxw = fl-max-width rasters 0 0
        in let gbase = fl-raster-to-gobf rasters maxw font-ppem
        in GopFont { gf-ok = True, gf-base = gbase, gf-gw = maxw, gf-gh = font-ppem }
      end
    end
  end

Section: Draw

 gbf-put-text wants a GopBuf; ours aliases the real framebuffer with
 the panel's stride standing as the buffer width, which is the only
 width gbf's pixel math uses.

  gfont-text : GopFont, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Text, Integer -> Integer
  gfont-text (f) (base) (stride) (h) (x) (y) (s) (fg) =
    gbf-put-text (GopBuf { gb-base = base, gb-width = stride, gb-height = h }) (f.gf-base) (f.gf-gw) (f.gf-gh) x y s fg
